# BuildKit picks up this file when building with container/Dockerfile and
# uses it instead of any .dockerignore at the context root. Patterns are
# relative to the build context (the parent dir containing LUCiD/ and
# PhotonSim/).
#
# Goal: keep the COPY layers' checksums stable across host-side build
# artifacts and editor/pytest scratch, so Docker's layer cache survives
# local rebuilds and the ~5 min PhotonSim compile doesn't rerun when
# only build artifacts change.

# Source-tree build output (most important: PhotonSim/build/ gets wiped
# inside the image anyway by Dockerfile:67, but keeping it out of the
# COPY checksum avoids pointless cache invalidation).
**/build/

# VCS metadata — Dockerfile sets SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION so we
# don't need .git inside the image for version inference.
**/.git/
**/.github/
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes

# Python packaging/test scratch
**/*.egg-info/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editor / OS scratch
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.claude/

# Local dev outputs that have no business being baked into the image
**/output/
**/generated_data/
**/test_events/
**/trained_model/
**/siren_training/
**/debug/

# Fetched example data. `COPY LUCiD /opt/LUCiD` otherwise bakes whatever
# scripts/download_data.py left in data/ into a published image — ~2.8 GB of
# ROOT per particle here, and data nobody agreed to redistribute. No *.root or
# *.h5 is tracked, so these patterns cost the build nothing. The SIREN weights
# are fetched like the ROOT files; the small tracked emitter.json files beside
# them are deliberately still copied.
**/*.root
**/*.h5
data/*/*/*/weights.npz

# Credentials and personal state. user_paths.sh is untracked by design (the
# three .template files say so) and carries a developer's absolute paths and
# account names. It does not belong in an image published to ghcr.io.
**/user_paths.sh
**/.netrc
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/id_rsa*
